Id: lin041i
Severity: INFO
Category: kernel
Check: check_sysctl
References: sysctl.d(5), systemd-sysctl(8)

Auditing a system that is not running (tigris --root), the kernel and
network settings are read from what it applies at boot: its sysctl.d
files and sysctl.conf. The settings listed are hardening ones that
nothing there sets, so they take the kernel's own default when it boots,
and that depends on the kernel: its version, how it was configured and
what its distribution changed. Some kernels default to the safe value
and some do not; Tigris cannot know which this one will boot.

To be sure, set each in a file of /etc/sysctl.d (for example
/etc/sysctl.d/90-hardening.conf) to the value the live check wants.
